    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by high-ceiling matchups, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Junior Caminero** (74.02). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly; the projection reflects a massive +19% boost due to the starter's skill level and a favorable +14% dynamic platoon advantage, making him our primary target for stolen bases. **Junior Caminero** also commands a high score despite facing a veteran arm like Framber Valdez, as the +11% cumulative lift from park factors and batting order confirms he is a must-start in the utility slot to anchor our middle-order production.\n\nSecondary pieces like **Lars Nootbaar** (58.28) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.89) provide stable scoring floors, with **Lars Nootbaar** finding value via a +11% platoon edge against Kevin Gausman, which offsets the difficulty of the matchup. On the bench, **Dillon Dingler** (37.61) was the final man squeezed out of the starting nine. While **Dillon Dingler** carries a solid projection, his -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Drew Rasmussen made it impossible to displace our starters, leading the optimizer to favor the higher upside of **Colt Keith** or **Trea Turner** despite the latter facing a tough arm in Logan Gilbert.\n\nManagers should note that all evaluations are predicated on \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Colt Keith**, **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, or **Chase Meidroth** drop down the order following official lineup releases, their efficiency scores will likely slide. We are avoiding the temptation to force **Dillon Dingler** into the lineup given the scarcity of our target categories, choosing instead to protect our remaining game caps. With **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** sidelined by team off-days, our active roster must capitalize on the aggressive projections assigned to **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Junior Caminero** to maintain our momentum in the standings.",
